#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# percent_form

#% text
# `percent_form(x)` shows the number `x` as a percentage: `0.35` as 35%; `percent_form(x, n)` with `n` significant digits.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `percent_form` stays around the value as a display wrapper. The wrapper stays around the value: it is a display directive and changes no computation.

#% item
# The displayed percentage is `100 x`; the value of `x` itself is not changed.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
percent_form(0.35)
#% output
#= percent_form(0.35)

#% cell
percent_form(2/3)
#% output
#= percent_form(2/3)

#% cell
percent_form(0.123456789, 4)
#% output
#= percent_form(0.123456789, 4)

#% cell
percent_form([0.1, 0.25, 0.5])
#% output
#= percent_form([0.1, 0.25, 0.5])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `number_form`, `decimal_form`, `scientific_form`
